From: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: nf_flow_table_path: handle DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA

Rebase of the old 675-03 onto kernel 6.18.41: mainline commit 93d7a7ed0734
moved the flowtable path-discovery machinery out of nft_flow_offload.c into
net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c. The DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA case (needed so
flows egressing to a WiFi/WDMA netdev get a valid source MAC and can be
HW-offloaded by the airoha PPE) was never mainlined, so re-add it in the
new file. Without it, WiFi-egress flows fall back to the CPU (PPE bind
table empty, high CPU, ~half throughput on WiFi downloads).

675-01 (symbol exports) + 675-02 (bridging) are now in mainline; 675-04
(vlan passthrough) is superseded by mainline's DEV_PATH_BR_VLAN_* handling.

---
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c	2026-08-02 16:22:13.779537237 +1000
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c	2026-08-02 16:22:19.672750332 +1000
@@ -157,6 +157,10 @@
 			}
 			info->xmit_type = FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_DIRECT;
 			break;
+		case DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA:
+			if (is_zero_ether_addr(info->h_source))
+				memcpy(info->h_source, path->dev->dev_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+			break;
 		default:
 			info->indev = NULL;
 			break;
